1
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,309
Two clocks.

2
00:00:08,834 --> 00:00:10,021
Two places.

3
00:00:10,546 --> 00:00:11,658
One moment.

4
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:18,322
It feels like the simplest idea in the world:

5
00:00:18,322 --> 00:00:21,210
everyone, everywhere, shares the same now.

6
00:00:22,817 --> 00:00:24,246
It is not simple.

7
00:00:24,771 --> 00:00:27,289
And strictly speaking, it is not true.

8
00:00:29,392 --> 00:00:35,665
In 1905, Einstein began with two facts that had been measured, but not understood.

9
00:00:36,617 --> 00:00:41,503
The laws of physics look the same to anyone moving at constant velocity.

10
00:00:41,953 --> 00:00:47,410
And light, in empty space, always moves at the same speed, whoever is measuring it.

11
00:00:48,825 --> 00:00:52,026
Hold on to both at once, and something has to give.

12
00:00:52,401 --> 00:00:54,919
What gives is the idea of a shared now.

13
00:00:55,425 --> 00:00:59,799
Picture a flash of light released from the exact middle of a moving ship.

14
00:01:00,099 --> 00:01:04,622
For someone on board, it reaches the front and the back at the same instant.

15
00:01:06,133 --> 00:01:10,405
For someone watching the ship pass, the back wall rushes toward the light,

16
00:01:10,405 --> 00:01:12,598
and the front wall runs away from it.

17
00:01:12,898 --> 00:01:15,027
The flash reaches the back first.

18
00:01:17,133 --> 00:01:18,777
Neither of them is wrong.

19
00:01:19,227 --> 00:01:22,818
The order of distant events depends on how you are moving,

20
00:01:22,818 --> 00:01:26,099
and no experiment can settle which of them is right.

21
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:32,631
Follow the consequences, and the familiar structure of time comes apart.

22
00:01:33,592 --> 00:01:38,286
A moving clock ticks more slowly, as measured by someone it moves past.

23
00:01:38,736 --> 00:01:42,171
A moving ruler is shorter along its direction of travel.

24
00:01:42,621 --> 00:01:45,246
These are not illusions. They are measurements.

25
00:01:45,558 --> 00:01:49,390
To see why, physicists draw a map that no one can walk on.

26
00:01:49,690 --> 00:01:52,891
Space along one axis. Time along the other.

27
00:01:53,191 --> 00:01:55,600
Light travels at forty-five degrees.

28
00:01:56,883 --> 00:02:00,553
Every clock traces a line through this map: its world line.

29
00:02:00,928 --> 00:02:04,108
And everything that can ever influence an event,

30
00:02:04,108 --> 00:02:07,819
or be influenced by it, lies inside two cones of light.

31
00:02:09,175 --> 00:02:14,616
Outside the cones lies a vast region of events that are neither before nor after.

32
00:02:14,991 --> 00:02:17,488
For them, 'now' is simply not defined.

33
00:02:19,050 --> 00:02:22,741
Change your velocity, and the slice you call 'the present' tilts.

34
00:02:23,191 --> 00:02:26,512
What happens 'at the same time' on a distant star is,

35
00:02:26,512 --> 00:02:29,144
quite literally, a matter of perspective.

36
00:02:30,050 --> 00:02:33,443
This is not philosophy. It is measured every day.

37
00:02:33,818 --> 00:02:37,470
Clocks aboard GPS satellites gain about thirty-eight

38
00:02:37,470 --> 00:02:40,560
microseconds a day on clocks on the ground.

39
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:45,405
Left uncorrected, your position would drift by kilometers within a day.

40
00:02:47,317 --> 00:02:49,039
So light sets the rules.

41
00:02:49,264 --> 00:02:52,913
Follow a single pulse, and you can measure the universe with it.

42
00:02:54,183 --> 00:02:58,813
Across an atom, it takes less than a billionth of a billionth of a second.

43
00:03:00,283 --> 00:03:03,569
Across a human body, a few billionths of a second.

44
00:03:05,575 --> 00:03:08,477
Around the Earth, seven times in one second.

45
00:03:11,867 --> 00:03:14,147
To the Moon, a little over a second.

46
00:03:14,372 --> 00:03:16,110
To the Sun, eight minutes.

47
00:03:16,335 --> 00:03:18,686
To the Voyager probes, most of a day.

48
00:03:25,158 --> 00:03:27,230
To the nearest star, four years.

49
00:03:27,455 --> 00:03:30,464
Across our galaxy, a hundred thousand years.

50
00:03:30,689 --> 00:03:34,530
To the farthest light we can see, more than thirteen billion years.

51
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:42,753
Every image of the sky is a layered photograph of different pasts.

52
00:03:43,128 --> 00:03:45,582
There is no single 'now' out there to look at.

53
00:03:45,882 --> 00:03:47,138
There never was.

54
00:03:50,442 --> 00:03:52,871
Then Einstein asked a harder question.

55
00:03:53,171 --> 00:03:56,180
What happens to this map when gravity is present?

56
00:03:57,217 --> 00:03:58,967
His answer took ten years.

57
00:03:59,342 --> 00:04:02,296
Gravity is not a force pulling through space.

58
00:04:02,296 --> 00:04:05,316
It is the shape of space and time themselves.

59
00:04:08,217 --> 00:04:10,415
Mass tells spacetime how to curve.

60
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:13,115
Curved spacetime tells mass how to move.

61
00:04:17,217 --> 00:04:19,817
A planet in orbit is not being pulled.

62
00:04:20,042 --> 00:04:24,096
It is travelling as straight as it can through a geometry that is bent.

63
00:04:25,217 --> 00:04:26,588
Light bends too.

64
00:04:26,888 --> 00:04:31,462
A galaxy behind a massive cluster is smeared into arcs and rings:

65
00:04:31,462 --> 00:04:33,502
a lens made of pure gravity.

66
00:04:37,217 --> 00:04:41,890
And clocks run at different rates depending on where they sit in that geometry.

67
00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:45,540
Deeper in a gravitational well, time runs slower.

68
00:04:45,915 --> 00:04:47,885
In 2010, two atomic clocks,

69
00:04:47,885 --> 00:04:53,724
one raised just thirty-three centimeters above the other, measurably disagreed.

70
00:04:56,958 --> 00:04:59,925
Compress enough mass into a small enough region,

71
00:04:59,925 --> 00:05:04,809
and there is a boundary from which no path leads back out. Not even for light.

72
00:05:05,259 --> 00:05:07,289
We call it the event horizon.

73
00:05:09,758 --> 00:05:12,340
This image is computed, not painted.

74
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:15,029
Every pixel is a path of light,

75
00:05:15,029 --> 00:05:18,613
traced through the geometry Karl Schwarzschild

76
00:05:18,613 --> 00:05:21,963
derived from Einstein's equations in 1916.

77
00:05:23,467 --> 00:05:26,241
Hot gas spirals inward in a thin disk.

78
00:05:26,541 --> 00:05:30,351
Light from the far side of the disk is bent up and over the hole,

79
00:05:30,351 --> 00:05:32,110
so you see what is behind it.

80
00:05:35,467 --> 00:05:38,108
The side rotating toward you is brighter.

81
00:05:38,408 --> 00:05:42,168
The gas there moves at a good fraction of the speed of light;

82
00:05:42,168 --> 00:05:45,373
its glow is beamed forward and shifted toward blue.

83
00:05:47,467 --> 00:05:50,141
And around the shadow, a thin bright ring:

84
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:53,388
light that circled the black hole before escaping.

85
00:05:53,838 --> 00:05:54,553
In 2019,

86
00:05:54,553 --> 00:06:01,976
the Event Horizon Telescope saw that ring around the black hole in the galaxy M87;

87
00:06:01,976 --> 00:06:06,447
in 2022, around the one at the center of our own.

88
00:06:08,092 --> 00:06:13,277
At the horizon, seen from far away, a falling clock seems to slow, and stop.

89
00:06:13,802 --> 00:06:17,301
For the one who falls, nothing special marks the crossing.

90
00:06:17,751 --> 00:06:19,693
Both descriptions are correct.

91
00:06:20,068 --> 00:06:21,853
There is no now they could share.

92
00:06:24,358 --> 00:06:26,867
While relativity was redrawing the large,

93
00:06:26,867 --> 00:06:29,927
a different revolution was dismantling the small.

94
00:06:30,967 --> 00:06:35,170
An electron in an atom is not a tiny planet on a tiny orbit.

95
00:06:35,545 --> 00:06:38,812
It is better described by a wave of possibility:

96
00:06:38,812 --> 00:06:42,351
a cloud whose shape is the solution of an equation.

97
00:06:43,717 --> 00:06:47,408
Where the wave is dense, the electron is likely to be found.

98
00:06:47,708 --> 00:06:50,443
Where it cancels itself, it is never found.

99
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:52,536
Interference, not orbit.

100
00:06:53,050 --> 00:06:57,318
A quantum system can be in a superposition: not here or there,

101
00:06:57,318 --> 00:07:02,757
but a precise blend of both, with amplitudes that add and subtract like waves.

102
00:07:03,357 --> 00:07:06,099
Measure it, and you get one definite answer.

103
00:07:06,399 --> 00:07:10,773
Repeat it, and the answers follow the probabilities the wave predicted.

104
00:07:12,258 --> 00:07:15,971
And some pairs of questions cannot both have sharp answers.

105
00:07:16,271 --> 00:07:21,008
The more precisely a position is fixed, the less precisely momentum can be.

106
00:07:21,308 --> 00:07:25,298
This is not a limit of instruments. It is a property of waves.

107
00:07:27,358 --> 00:07:31,924
Now take two particles, prepared together, so that their properties are linked.

108
00:07:32,883 --> 00:07:35,081
Send one to a laboratory on Earth.

109
00:07:35,306 --> 00:07:37,682
Send the other across the solar system.

110
00:07:42,883 --> 00:07:45,785
Measure each one, and its answer is random.

111
00:07:46,085 --> 00:07:48,844
Compare them, and they match, every time,

112
00:07:48,844 --> 00:07:53,083
in ways no story of hidden, pre-arranged values can reproduce.

113
00:07:53,383 --> 00:07:55,520
That is what Bell's theorem proves,

114
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:59,122
and what experiments have confirmed, loophole by loophole.

115
00:08:00,467 --> 00:08:02,852
But look carefully at what did not happen.

116
00:08:03,227 --> 00:08:05,100
Nothing travelled between them.

117
00:08:05,475 --> 00:08:10,165
No one on Earth can choose which answer the distant particle gives.

118
00:08:10,165 --> 00:08:13,945
So: no message, no signal, nothing faster than light.

119
00:08:14,395 --> 00:08:18,525
Entanglement is a correlation written into the state of the pair.

120
00:08:18,525 --> 00:08:20,241
It cannot carry a message.

121
00:08:22,358 --> 00:08:26,177
So we arrive at the strangest situation in modern science.

122
00:08:27,217 --> 00:08:31,520
On one side, general relativity: gravity as geometry.

123
00:08:31,820 --> 00:08:36,230
It predicted the bending of starlight, the slowing of clocks,

124
00:08:36,230 --> 00:08:40,930
black holes, and the gravitational waves first detected in 2015.

125
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:44,588
On the other, quantum field theory:

126
00:08:44,588 --> 00:08:48,315
particles as excitations of fields filling all of space.

127
00:08:48,615 --> 00:08:53,394
It predicts the magnetism of the electron to twelve decimal places.

128
00:08:54,758 --> 00:08:58,896
Each works, in its domain, to a precision that is almost absurd.

129
00:08:58,896 --> 00:09:01,223
But they speak different languages.

130
00:09:01,673 --> 00:09:07,327
In relativity, spacetime is a smooth, dynamic stage, shaped by the matter on it.

131
00:09:07,552 --> 00:09:11,926
In quantum theory, the stage is fixed, and the actors are uncertain.

132
00:09:13,258 --> 00:09:17,449
Try to make gravity itself quantum, the way the other forces are,

133
00:09:17,449 --> 00:09:22,155
and the calculations fill with infinities the usual methods cannot tame.

134
00:09:22,605 --> 00:09:27,590
At ordinary energies this is harmless: each theory is used where it applies.

135
00:09:27,965 --> 00:09:30,035
But at the center of a black hole,

136
00:09:30,035 --> 00:09:34,174
and in the first instant of the universe, both must matter at once.

137
00:09:34,474 --> 00:09:37,696
There, our best descriptions stop making predictions.

138
00:09:40,867 --> 00:09:43,746
What is reality made of, at the deepest level?

139
00:09:44,646 --> 00:09:45,851
We do not know.

140
00:09:46,301 --> 00:09:47,351
Not yet.

141
00:09:49,133 --> 00:09:50,926
There are serious candidates.

142
00:09:51,226 --> 00:09:52,320
String theory.

143
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:54,242
Loop quantum gravity.

144
00:09:54,542 --> 00:09:59,046
Ideas in which space and time themselves emerge from something deeper,

145
00:09:59,046 --> 00:10:02,777
the way temperature emerges from the motion of molecules.

146
00:10:05,133 --> 00:10:09,528
None of them has yet made a prediction that experiment has confirmed.

147
00:10:09,828 --> 00:10:12,986
They are not established physics. They are the frontier.

148
00:10:14,467 --> 00:10:16,324
What is established is this.

149
00:10:16,774 --> 00:10:18,631
There is no universal now.

150
00:10:19,006 --> 00:10:22,377
Time is local, and relative, and shaped by mass.

151
00:10:22,752 --> 00:10:26,063
At the smallest scales, reality is probabilistic,

152
00:10:26,063 --> 00:10:30,049
and correlated in ways that have no classical explanation.

153
00:10:30,424 --> 00:10:32,097
And our two best theories,

154
00:10:32,097 --> 00:10:36,279
each confirmed beyond reasonable doubt, do not yet fit together.

155
00:10:39,008 --> 00:10:40,950
So return to the first clock.

156
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:44,326
Are these two events happening at the same time?

157
00:10:46,508 --> 00:10:49,579
The question that seemed trivial was never trivial.

158
00:10:49,954 --> 00:10:53,624
It depends on where you stand, how you move, and what you are near.

159
00:10:54,149 --> 00:10:58,843
And the universe, as far as we can tell, keeps no single time for anyone.

